# An exported class is the route of its doors: building it and each public method, each called by the entry: the
# methods run on the caller's instance, `Store` from beyond, and what the building makes goes back to the caller. What
# a call changes in place, it gives: `rows.push(new Row(reading))` makes `rows` anew from the rows read and the Row
# built of the Reading, so the Reading reaches what is written at the place the store is made with,
# `Disk(Store.path)`. `get` builds the Readings back from the rows it reads: what goes in as a Reading comes out as
# one. The route reads the place and writes it again: it stands on both sides.

